CVA6ConfigDcacheLineWidth = 128 Signal Flow Tree (32KB 8-way Configuration)
===========================================================================

1. CONFIGURATION PHASE (cv32a6_imac_sv32_config_pkg.sv)
   └── localparam CVA6ConfigDcacheLineWidth = 128;
       └── cva6_cfg.'{ DcacheLineWidth: unsigned'(CVA6ConfigDcacheLineWidth) }

2. BUILD/DERIVATION PHASE (build_config_pkg.sv)
   └── CVA6Cfg.DcacheLineWidth = 128
       ├── DCACHE_LINE_WIDTH = CVA6Cfg.DcacheLineWidth = 128
       ├── DCACHE_OFFSET_WIDTH calculation:
       │   └── $clog2(CVA6Cfg.DcacheLineWidth / 8)
       │       └── $clog2(128 / 8) = $clog2(16) = 4 bits
       │
       └── DCACHE_USER_LINE_WIDTH calculation:
           └── (CVA6Cfg.AxiUserWidth == 1) ? 4 : CVA6Cfg.DcacheLineWidth
               └── 128 bits (assuming AxiUserWidth != 1)

3. MODULE INSTANTIATION PHASE
   └── std_cache_subsystem (core/cache_subsystem/std_cache_subsystem.sv)
       └── wt_dcache (core/cache_subsystem/wt_dcache.sv)
           └── wt_dcache_mem (core/cache_subsystem/wt_dcache_mem.sv)
               ├── parameter DCACHE_LINE_WIDTH = CONFIG.DCACHE_LINE_WIDTH = 128
               └── parameter DCACHE_OFFSET_WIDTH = CONFIG.DCACHE_OFFSET_WIDTH = 4

4. MEMORY ORGANIZATION IMPACT
   └── SRAM Data Width (wt_dcache_mem.sv)
       └── sram #(
           ├── .DATA_WIDTH(DCACHE_LINE_WIDTH) → 128 bits per cache line
           ├── .NUM_WORDS(DCACHE_NUM_WORDS) → 256 words per way
           └── Each SRAM stores 128-bit cache lines

5. ADDRESS DECODING IMPACT
   └── Address field extraction:
       ├── Offset field: addr[DCACHE_OFFSET_WIDTH-1:0] → addr[3:0]
       │   └── Selects byte within 16-byte cache line
       ├── Index field: addr[DCACHE_INDEX_WIDTH+DCACHE_OFFSET_WIDTH-1:DCACHE_OFFSET_WIDTH]
       │   └── addr[15:4] → 12-bit index for 4096 sets
       └── Tag field: addr[PLEN-1:DCACHE_INDEX_WIDTH+DCACHE_OFFSET_WIDTH]
           └── addr[31:16] → 16-bit tag

6. DATA PATH IMPACT
   └── Cache Line Operations:
       ├── Read data path: 128-bit cache line → CPU word extraction
       │   └── Byte/halfword/word selection within 128-bit line
       ├── Write data path: CPU data → 128-bit cache line update
       │   └── Byte enable logic for partial line writes
       ├── Fill operations: AXI memory → 128-bit cache line refill
       └── Write buffer: Stores 128-bit lines for write-through

7. AXI INTERFACE IMPACT (wt_axi_adapter.sv)
   └── AXI Data Width Conversion:
       ├── AXI data width: 64 bits (typical)
       ├── Cache line width: 128 bits
       └── Burst operations: 2 AXI beats per cache line
           ├── Beat 0: addr[63:0] → cache_line[63:0]
           └── Beat 1: addr[127:64] → cache_line[127:64]

8. BYTE ENABLE LOGIC
   └── Write mask generation:
       ├── CPU byte enables → 128-bit cache line byte enables
       ├── 16 byte enable bits (one per byte in line)
       ├── Offset-based byte enable shifting
       └── Partial line write support for WT cache

9. PERFORMANCE IMPACT (32KB Configuration)
   └── 128-bit Cache Lines in 32KB Cache:
       ├── Total lines: 32768 / 16 = 2048 cache lines
       ├── Good spatial locality exploitation
       ├── Efficient memory bandwidth utilization
       ├── 2-beat AXI transfers optimize bus usage
       └── Matches typical memory subsystem width

10. CACHE LINE CALCULATIONS
    └── Line Organization in 32KB 8-way:
        ├── Lines per way: 256
        ├── Bytes per line: 16
        ├── Words per line: 4 (32-bit words)
        ├── Total lines: 256 × 8 = 2048
        └── Address bits per line: 4 (offset bits)

KEY RELATIONSHIPS:
- DcacheLineWidth = 128 bits = 16 bytes defines cache granularity
- OFFSET_WIDTH = 4 bits addresses 16 bytes within line
- Optimal for 32-bit RISC-V: 4 instructions per line
- Standard line size for embedded caches
- Balances spatial locality vs cache pollution